@page "/"
@using Microsoft.Extensions.Options
@inject IOptions<SmartOptions> Smart
@{
    ViewData["Title"] = "Launch this app from an EHR";
    var learnUrl = Smart.Value.Url("/learn");
}

<p>This app has nothing to show on its own — it waits to be launched by an EHR.</p>

<ol>
    <li>Open the <a href="https://launch.smarthealthit.org/">SMART App Launcher</a>.</li>
    <li>Set <strong>Launch Type</strong> to <em>Provider EHR Launch</em> and <strong>FHIR Version</strong> to <em>R4</em>.</li>
    <li>Paste the URL below into <strong>App's Launch URL</strong>, and leave Client ID and Redirect URIs blank.</li>
    <li>Pick a patient, then press <strong>Launch</strong>.</li>
</ol>

<section class="step">
    <h2><code>@learnUrl</code></h2>
    <p>
        A real launch, narrated. It stops at each step to show what was sent, what came
        back, and why — the issuer check, discovery, the authorization request, PKCE, the
        token exchange, and the patient read — and ends on the patient summary the whole
        handshake was for.
    </p>
</section>
